<title>NORWAY: TABLE-NYCOMED H1 PROFITS FALL.</title>
<headline>TABLE-NYCOMED H1 PROFITS FALL.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>				(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Sales revenues		   3,977    vs     3,991</p>
<p> Operating result		   724    vs	 772</p>
<p> Pre-tax income		     604    vs	 678</p>
<p> Net income			   399    vs	 448</p>
<p> Net financial items	minus 120   vs   minus 94</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Norway's largest pharmaceuticals group is Nycomed ASA. The company was expected to present first-half 1997 pre-tax profits of 563 million crowns, according to a consensus poll of eight analysts by Reuters.</p>
<p>Nycomed announced on July 1 that it plans to merge with Britain's Amersham International Plc.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
